-- title:
--   Constructible sets contain points of the closure generising them
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a topological space and let $s \subseteq X$ be constructible in the sense of Mathlib's `Topology.IsConstructible`, i.e. $s$ belongs to the Boolean subalgebra of subsets of $X$ generated by the open retrocompact sets (an open $U$ being retrocompact when $U \cap K$ is compact for every open compact $K \subseteq X$). Let $x \in X$ be a point lying in the closure of $s$ and suppose that $x$ specialises to every point of $s$: for all $y \in s$ one has $x \rightsquigarrow y$, that is, $\mathcal{N}_x \le \mathcal{N}_y$, equivalently $y \in \overline{\{x\}}$, equivalently every open set containing $y$ contains $x$. Then $x \in s$. No separation, quasi-compactness or spectrality hypothesis on $X$ is imposed, and no hypothesis that $s$ be nonempty is needed (it follows from $x \in \overline{s}$ in the nontrivial branch of the argument).
--
--   This is the standard criterion, used for constructible sets in schemes, that a constructible set contains any generisation of all of its points that lies in its closure; the classical case is that of the generic point of an irreducible closed subset meeting the closure of $s$. It is used here in the proof of [`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_image_of_mem_closure_image_of_forall_specializes`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.mem_image_of_mem_closure_image_of_forall_specializes).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Topology_IsConstructible_mem_of_mem_closure_of_forall_specializes.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open Topology

universe u

theorem Topology.IsConstructible.mem_of_mem_closure_of_forall_specializes
    {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] {s : Set X} (hs : Topology.IsConstructible s)
    {x : X} (hx : x ∈ closure s) (hgen : ∀ y ∈ s, x ⤳ y) : x ∈ s := by sorry
